# Dependency names the base b1nix image already satisfies.
#
# Alpine states its dependencies as virtual tokens ("so:libc.musl-x86_64.so.1",
# "/bin/sh"), and resolving those against the index would pull in Alpine's own
# musl and BusyBox — packages whose files are the running system's libc, dynamic
# loader and shell. Installing them would overwrite the machine underneath the
# process doing the installing.
#
# Every entry here is a dependency that is genuinely met, not one being ignored:
# b1nix builds musl 1.2.5 (the same release Alpine v3.20 ships) and BusyBox from
# source. A token that does NOT appear here and is not in any index is reported
# as an unresolved dependency, not skipped silently.
#
# One token per line, matched exactly.

# libc + dynamic loader: build/x86_64/rootfs/lib/ld-musl-x86_64.so.1 (musl 1.2.5)
musl
so:libc.musl-x86_64.so.1
musl-utils
scanelf
ld-linux

# shell + coreutils: /opt/busybox/bin/busybox, linked from /bin/sh and /bin/ash
busybox
busybox-binsh
/bin/sh
/bin/ash
alpine-baselayout
alpine-baselayout-data

# init: BusyBox init as PID 1 with OpenRC driving the runlevels (M108)
openrc
